# [Declaration and registration]($heading.id('declaration-and-registration'))

```zig
const greeting = phpz.ini.string.new(.{
    .name = "my_php_extension.greeting",
    .default = "Hello",
    .access = .all,
});

const workers = phpz.ini.int.new(.{
    .name = "my_php_extension.workers",
    .default = 4,
    .access = .all,
});

const debug = phpz.ini.boolean.new(.{
    .name = "my_php_extension.debug",
    .default = false,
    .access = .all,
});
```

Add the definitions to `phpz.module` as `.ini = &.{ greeting, workers, debug }`. phpz registers them at module startup and unregisters them at shutdown.

# [Read values]($heading.id('read-values'))

Read the settings in a handler:

```zig
ctx.ret(.string, try greeting.get());
```

String results borrow the current configuration data. Copy the bytes before retaining them across configuration changes.

| Access | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `.system` | System-level configuration |
| `.user` | User-level configuration, writable from scripts with `ini_set()` |
| `.perdir` | Per-directory configuration, set in `php.ini` or the SAPI's directory configuration |
| `.all` | All configuration levels |

PHP's INI access level controls which settings can be changed with `php -d`, `php.ini` and `ini_set()`.

# [Custom types and bindings]($heading.id('custom-types-and-bindings'))

`phpz.ini.Typed(T).new` takes `parse`, `format` and `default_text` and can map text to a Zig enum. `.bind = Globals.iniField("mode")` binds the parsed result to a module globals field.

Use `get()` to read the field for the current thread. On a parse failure, return an error and preserve the previous state.

# [phpinfo() displayers]($heading.id('phpinfo-displayers'))

Scalar and `Typed` INI entries accept `.displayer`. Adapt the callback for Zend with `phpz.ini.displayer(callback)`:

```zig
fn displayDebug(entry: *phpz.c.zend_ini_entry, kind: phpz.ini.DisplayType) void {
    const modified = if (comptime @TypeOf(entry.modified) == bool) entry.modified else entry.modified != 0;
    const value = if (kind == .original and modified) entry.orig_value else entry.value;
    const text = if (value) |str| phpz.zend.String.from(str).slice() else "";
    const label: [:0]const u8 = if (phpz.ini.parseBool(text)) "on" else "off";
    _ = phpz.printf("%s", .{label.ptr});
}

const debug = phpz.ini.boolean.new(.{
    .name = "my_php_extension.debug",
    .default = false,
    .access = .all,
    .displayer = phpz.ini.displayer(displayDebug),
});
```

The callback receives the INI entry and a `DisplayType`. `.active` requests the effective value. For `.original`, inspect `modified` and use `orig_value` when the setting has changed. The representation of `modified` varies between PHP versions around 8.6. Check the headers for a bool or integer.

A displayer writes directly to phpinfo output with `phpz.printf`. Escape dynamic text before including it in HTML. In a custom `info_fn`, call [phpz.info.ini(module)]($link.page('reference/runtime/output').ref('extension-information')) to list the module's INI entries. PHP lists them automatically with its default information output when the module declares a version.
